      <title>Sheeba Chaddha on embracing truth in acting and her role in Riz Ahmed's Hamlet</title>
      <link>https://www.indulgexpress.com/entertainment/celebs/2026/Feb/22/sheeba-chaddha-on-embracing-truth-in-acting-and-her-role-in-riz-ahmeds-hamlet</link>
      <description>Sheeba Chaddha, known for her nuanced performances, discusses her approach to acting, emphasizing the importance of truth in her roles. In Riz Ahmed's adaptation of Hamlet, she portrays Gertrude, a character she views through a universal lens rather than a strictly South Asian one. Chaddha reflects on the evolution of motherhood roles in Bollywood, highlighting the shift from passive to more dynamic portrayals, and shares her gratitude for the organic journey of her career.</description>
