      <title>These collections reinterpret Indian rituals and gathering spaces through concrete and terrazzo</title>
      <link>https://www.indulgexpress.com/mlaunches/home-and-decor/2026/Feb/22/these-collections-reinterpret-indian-rituals-and-gathering-spaces-through-concrete-and-terrazzo</link>
      <description>Parman Designs' latest collections, Agami and Baithak, reinterpret Indian rituals and gathering spaces through innovative use of concrete and terrazzo. Agami looks forward, abstracting traditional forms into contemporary silhouettes with bold geometry, while Baithak draws on the social essence of traditional Indian gathering spaces. Both collections emphasize storytelling and cultural memory, creating meaningful, emotionally resonant pieces for modern homes.</description>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.indulgexpress.com/mlaunches/home-and-decor/2026/Feb/22/these-collections-reinterpret-indian-rituals-and-gathering-spaces-through-concrete-and-terrazzo</guid>
